      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how Grimoire\u0027s guarded write path uses an in-memory journal to enable transaction-like semantics for file writes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core mechanism**: Before any file is overwritten, the system records its prior state in a write journal \u2014 either saving the previous content if the file existed, or noting that it didn\u0027t exist yet.\n\n**Rollback on failure**: If the agent run fails (due to turn cap limits, unrecoverable errors, or denied write attempts), the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order \u2014 restoring original content for modified files and deleting newly created ones.\n\n**All-or-nothing semantics**: This design provides transaction-like guarantees without needing a database \u2014 the in-memory journal itself acts as the transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Scope note**: The page clarifies that the Query agent (which has no write capability) never uses the journal\u0027s rollback functionality, even though the journal type exists in the shared runtime library.",
